        {
          "display": "<p>The pictogram below shows the number of passengers on four train routes. A single symbol is used per row, but the symbols are drawn at different sizes proportional to the number of passengers. Which statement best describes why this is a misleading representation?</p><svg class=\"pictogram\" viewBox=\"0 0 460 220\" width=\"100%\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><text x=\"80\" y=\"29\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-family=\"Inter,sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\">Route 1</text><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"25\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"29\" font-family=\"Inter,sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#555\">= 80 passengers</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"79\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-family=\"Inter,sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\">Route 2</text><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"75\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"79\" font-family=\"Inter,sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#555\">= 160 passengers</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"129\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-family=\"Inter,sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\">Route 3</text><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"125\" r=\"17\" fill=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"129\" font-family=\"Inter,sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#555\">= 240 passengers</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"179\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-family=\"Inter,sans-serif\" font-size=\"13\">Route 4</text><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"175\" r=\"22\" fill=\"#7c3aed\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"179\" font-family=\"Inter,sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#555\">= 320 passengers</text></svg>",
          "options": [
