        {
          "display": "<table class=\"data-table\"><tr><th>Format</th><th>Advantages</th><th>Disadvantages</th></tr><tr><td>Tally chart</td><td>Fast to record live data</td><td>Hard to read totals quickly</td></tr><tr><td>Frequency table</td><td>Clear totals and comparisons</td><td>Data already collected — not live</td></tr><tr><td>Pictogram</td><td>Visual appeal for non-specialists</td><td>Hard to represent non-multiples of key</td></tr></table><br>A researcher needs to count vehicles passing a junction every 30 seconds over one hour, then present the results to a general audience. Which two formats would best serve these two purposes respectively?",
